ith a small longest-match script (not `urllib.robotparser`, which uses first-match):\n- Allowed: `/v1/notes`, `/v1/notes?limit=50`, `/v1/notes/<slug>`.\n- Blocked: `/v1/notes/x/reactions`, `/v1/me`, `/v1/me/drafts`, `/v1/auth/token`, `/admin/`.\n\nNothing was deployed. After deploying:\n1. Run `curl -s https://fieldnotes.example/robots.txt` to confirm the live file.\n2. In Search Console, request a robots.txt recrawl.\n3. Run URL Inspection → Test live URL on `/n/drip-line-pressure`, and request indexing.\n\n## Recommended follow-ups (not done)\n- Make `app.js` show a real error when the API fetch fails, and don't call it \"not found\" when the cause was a network or API error. Better, have the server return a real 404 status for unknown slugs.\n- Put plain `<a href=\"/n/...\">` links in the homepage HTML at build time, so discovery doesn't depend on JavaScript.\n","structuredPatch":[],"originalFile":null,"userModified":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01L4Pk4sRUWGnrMeFuTz65z5","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgAp76vxVK8TpkE8Hjscz","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The soft 404s come from `Disallow: /v1/` in `site/robots.txt`. I've changed that file and written the cause and fix up in `ANSWER.md`. Nothing is deployed or submitted.\n\n**Cause:** Each note page is a static shell. `app.js` fills it in by fetching `/v1/notes/<slug>`, and Googlebot obeys robots.txt when it renders. With that fetch blocked, `app.js` shows its \"NOT FOUND\" screen, served with HTTP 200, and Google classes that as a soft 404. The inspection file for `/n/drip-line-pressure` shows exactly this: the fetch succeeds, but the rendered text is \"NOT FOUND\". The CSV fits the timeline. Notes crawled in late August are indexed, and notes crawled in October are soft 404s.\n\n**Fix:** `site/robots.txt` now reads:\n\n```\nUser-agent: *\nDisallow: /v1/\nAllow: /v1/notes\nDisallow: /v1/notes/*/reactions\nDisallow: /admin/\n```\n\nThe public read endpoints are allowed. The reactions endpoint, `/v1/me`, `/v1/auth` and `/admin/` stay blocked. I checked this with a small longest-match script (not `urllib.robotparser`, which uses first-match). It allowed `/v1/notes`, `/v1/notes?limit=50` and `/v1/notes/<slug>`, and blocked the other five paths I tried.\n\nAfter you deploy, check the live file with `curl`, request a robots.txt recrawl in Search Console, then run Test live URL on `/n/drip-line-pressure`.\n\n`ANSWER.md` also lists two follow-ups I didn't make:\n- Make `app.js` show a real error, or return a real 404 status, instead of a 200 \"not found\" screen.\n- Write plain links to the notes into the homepage HTML at build time."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1931,"cache_read_input_tokens":23995,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1931},"output_tokens":634,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"00d0de85-2139-4ecb-8825-b91b3caa59f2","uuid":"cbf0e59a-7a80-4d18-a267-f17dba969a4e","timestamp":"2026-10-19T02:33:01.729Z","request_id":"req_011CgAp76fb1YTJjaG64uZEY"}
